    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0200" n="830" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg830"/>

                <head>No. 380.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General <persName corresp="#p_DES1"
                            type="from">Sickles</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="to">Fish</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                                States Legation in Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 11, 1872</date>.
                        (Received January 6, 1873.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 501.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward a translation
                    of an interpellation in the senate, and another in the chamber, respecting the
                    proposed sale of slaves in Cuba by the Spanish government, to which reference is
                    made in my No. 496. You will note with satisfaction the declaration of the
                    colonial minister that he has prohibited the sale. He fails, however, to state
                    that these slaves held by the government have been liberated, as required by the
                    law of July 4, 1870.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_DES1">D. E. SICKLES</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>




                <xi:include href="d54-a1.xml" xpointer="d54-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d54-a2.xml" xpointer="d54-a2"/>
